-- cpl_memory rows for SkyVireo (S682), the CPL Queue routine's 14:12Z firing of 2026-11-18, a light checkpoint
-- under the stop rule's stand-down. Applied by supabase-migrate.yml (kb/migrations/.apply), never Execute SQL.
-- INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING. Every row lands proposed. No new ruling from Sam in his own words this
-- run: COBIx's two relays on #3153 are recorded as COBIx's, and every row names the conductor.
-- ROLLBACK: kb/migrations/2026-11-18_s682_cpl_memory_rows_rollback.sql
insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('d-stand-down-firing-took-first-light-ask-s682','decision','A stand-down firing took the First Light ask COBIx relayed after the handoff','S682 conductor, under the stop rule''s stand-down from handoff 682: the 14:12Z firing took one ask outside the collection queue, First Light''s Apply on #3153, which COBIx relayed from Sam at 13:55Z, after the handoff was written. It started no read, load, apply or collection worker and did no UI or tooling work. Sam or COBIx may reverse this.',array['conductor','stop-rule','first-light','scheduled-sessions'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('d-first-light-paintings-half-only-s682','decision','First Light: #3511 carries the 77 painting drops alone','S682 conductor: #3511 carries the 77 painting drops Sam marked in the First Light tab (271 paintings to 194, marks consumed through id 90) and leaves out the 13 My CPL Story photo adds. Those stay live marks until the hero photo rule and the tab''s Add agree. Sam merges #3511; no session merges it.',array['first-light','sierra-page-redesign'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('d-receipt-checks-retire-after-tab-apply-s682','decision','The October gallery receipts stop governing the selection once a tab Apply lands','S682 conductor (#3511): once the tab''s Apply has landed, meaning tools/first_light_selection.json records a consumed mark id, the October gallery receipts no longer say what the selection should hold, so tests/first_light_picks_applied.test.js runs its checks (a) and (b) only before that.',array['first-light','tests'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('p-fixture-marks-spent-after-an-apply-s682','pitfall','Fixture marks with small ids read as spent after an Apply','S682 (#3511): first_light_needs_words and first_light_marks used fixture marks with ids 1 to 50. Once the committed lists record a consumed id of 90 (paintings) or 89 (photos), the Apply and the tab read those marks as spent, so the tests failed on any applied list. Start a fixture from a never-applied copy of the lists.',array['first-light','tests','pitfall'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('p-skip-ci-head-leaves-a-pr-without-test-s682','pitfall','A [skip ci] head leaves a First Light PR with no test check','S682: first-light-art.yml runs on a push to a claude/** branch that changes first_light.js and commits tools/first_light_verify.json back with [skip ci]. The PR head is then that commit, so no pull_request check runs. Start test by dispatching js-tests.yml on the branch (actions_run_trigger, run_workflow, ref the branch), as the Apply workflow does.',array['first-light','ci','merging','pitfall'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('f-first-light-apply-cannot-open-its-pr-s682','fact','First Light''s Apply builds its set and cannot open its pull request','S682 read: Apply requests 1 (2026-11-12, run 43355121683) and 2 (2026-11-17, run 44107318402) read failed with no PR link; each run built its set and failed at gh pr create: "GitHub Actions is not permitted to create or approve pull requests." COBIx relayed on #3153 (13:55Z 2026-11-18) that Sam chose not to turn that setting on. Ask B (a token stored as a secret) is open.',array['first-light','github-actions','sierra-page-redesign'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('f-hero-photo-rule-refuses-story-photos-s682','fact','The public pages'' hero rule refuses the My CPL Story photos the tab adds','S682 measured: tests/public_library.test.js (6e) wants every hero photo a 4:3 JPEG at most 1,200 px wide named photos/<name>.jpg; tests/public_adopt.test.js wants exactly 11 slides. The 13 story photos are PNGs and JPEGs, 126x152 to 2560x1920, nine under 400 px wide, 6.3 MB. The tab''s Add accepts what the pages refuse: a design call for a plain session.',array['first-light','library','hero-photos','design'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18'),
('m-search-issues-since-the-handoff-s682','procedure','Search issues and PRs updated since the handoff, even in a stand-down','S682: two gh api -X GET search/issues calls, is:pull-request and is:issue, each with updated:>=<the handoff or stop time>, list everything touched since the handoff. They found #3153, where COBIx had posted outside the brief. A stand-down firing still runs them to read for a word from Sam.',array['scheduled-sessions','conductor','procedure'],'proposed','#3511; #3153','SkyVireo (S682), the conductor',null,'SkyVireo (S682)',date '2026-11-18')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

